  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 5,
  "title": "Galatians 5",
  "display_title": "Galatians 5",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "galatians",
  "book": "Galatians",
  "bookName": "Galatians",
  "bookOrder": 48,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 5,
  "sortOrder": 48005,
  "verseCount": 26,
  "aliases": [
    "Gal",
    "Ga"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Stand fast therefore in the liberty wherewith Christ hath made us free, and be not entangled again with the yoke of bondage.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Behold, I Paul say unto you, that if ye be circumcised, Christ shall profit you nothing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For I testify again to every man that is circumcised, that he is a debtor to do the whole law.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Christ is become of no effect unto you, whosoever of you are justified by the law; ye are fallen from grace.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "For we through the Spirit wait for the hope of righteousness by faith.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "For in Jesus Christ neither circumcision availeth any thing, nor uncircumcision; but faith which worketh by love.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Ye did run well; who did hinder you that ye should not obey the truth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "This persuasion cometh not of him that calleth you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "A little leaven leaveneth the whole lump.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "I have confidence in you through the Lord, that ye will be none otherwise minded: but he that troubleth you shall bear his judgment, whosoever he be.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And I, brethren, if I yet preach circumcision, why do I yet suffer persecution? then is the offence of the cross ceased.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "I would they were even cut off which trouble you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "But if ye bite and devour one another, take heed that ye be not consumed one of another.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary the one to the other: so that ye cannot do the things that ye would.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "But if ye be led of the Spirit, ye are not under the law.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like: of the which I tell you before, as I have also told you in time past, that they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "And they that are Christ’s have crucified the flesh with the affections and lusts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "If we live in the Spirit, let us also walk in the Spirit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:galatians:5:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "Let us not be desirous of vain glory, provoking one another, envying one another.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Galatians 5:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:galatians:5:26"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
